This header needs to be updated

```
### Origin and review

TextProv records declared origin; it does not detect authorship.

- **Highlighted text was recorded as originating from AI output.** This happens during the
  development process and is integrated directly into the dev tools we use. It's at an early
  experimental stage and is not a perfect process. Content can still be highlighted after
  it's been reviewed by a person, so it doesn't mean that content is bad or low quality;
  just that those characters originated from AI output.
- **Text that isn't highlighted doesn't mean it was written by a person.** Older content
  was not labelled retroactively, so a page with no highlights can still contain earlier
  AI work.
- **The marks do not indicate review or accuracy.** They record how text was
  written, not whether someone has checked it or whether it is correct.
```

